# Modules & kernel (shared with WebinoDashboard)

## Module / submodule standard

- Every feature is a **module** or **submodule** with a manifest (frontend `modules/*/manifest.ts`, backend nwidart package + `manifest.json`).
- Register in the kernel registry (`frontend/src/kernel/registry.ts` + nwidart service provider). Enable/disable via license/activations — do not hard-wire routes that ignore activations.
- Admin page: `modules/{slug}/admin/{submodule}-page`.
- Public page: `modules/{slug}/site/{submodule}-page`.

```text
❌ BAD — dump a new page under features/ or src/views with no module/activation
✅ GOOD — manifest route + activation check + admin settings
```

Frontend module layout must match WebinoDashboard so UIs can be shared across products. Backend stays nwidart (`backend/Modules/{Name}/`).

## ERP domains

Canonical frontend slugs: `core`, `crm`, `accounting`, `hrm`, `projects`, `sales`, `scm`, `mfg`, `docs`, `integrations`, `marketplace`, `marketing`, `site-builder`.

## Public marketing site

- Marketing CMS lives in the `marketing` module (public `site/` pages).
- Theme chrome (if used) lives under `frontend/src/themes/{slug}/` and consumes branding from the API — never hard-code brand assets as the only option.

## Shared vs product-specific

- **Shared contract:** `ModuleManifest` types, kernel registry, shadcn shell, `@webina/ui`.
- **ERP-only:** Accounting, HRM, CRM, SiteBuilder provisioning, Integrations.
- Do not fork payment/SMS gateways per page — keep them in `integrations`.

## Everything configurable

- Logo, favicon, accent, colors, fonts, nav labels, contact info → admin settings / branding API.
- Front-end reads branding from the config/branding API, never embeds fixed brand assets as the only option.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fixed logo path with no settings
<img src="/brand/logo-fixed.png" />

// ✅ GOOD — from branding payload with fallback only for empty state
<SiteLogo logoUrl={branding.logo_url} siteName={siteName} />
```
